;; Clause 5.5.1 prints no table for its members and says "The
;; Requested-Information AVP is defined in ES 283 035 [11] while the
;; AF-Application-Identifier AVP is defined in TS 183 017 [10]", the two
;; documents the header's bases add to the base protocol.

; Specification: ETSI TS 183 020
; Version: 1.1.1
; Vendor-ID: 13019
; Bases: RFC6733, ETSI-ES283.035, ETSI-TS183.017
; Link: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/183000_183099/183020/01.01.01_60/ts_183020v010101p.pdf
; Transcribed: by hand from https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/183000_183099/183020/01.01.01_60/ts_183020v010101p.pdf


;; Table 1 maps information elements to Diameter attributes, printing no code,
;; type or flag rule, and heads its last column "Defined in". Its rows name the
;; elements SubscriberID, GloballyUniqueAddress, InitialGateSetting, QoSProfile
;; (NOTE 1) and PrivacyIndicator (see note), and Privacy-Indicator's cell reads
;; "The present document (clause 5.5.1)". The NOTE: This information element may
;; be repeated.
; Type: Reused AVPs
; Section: 5.5
; Table: 1
; Page: 13
; Columns: Name           From
User-Name                 RFC3588
Globally-Unique-Address   ETSI-ES283.034
Initiate-Gate-Setting     ETSI-ES283.034
QoS-Profile               ETSI-ES283.034
Privacy-Indicator         ETSI-TS183.020


;; No table of the document gives Privacy-Indicator's flag rules; the clause
;; states its code, vendor and type alone.
; Type: Grouped AVP
; Name: Privacy-Indicator
; Section: 5.5.1
; Page: 14
Privacy-Indicator ::= < AVP Header: 440 13019 >
      * { Requested-Information }
      * [ AF-Application-Identifier ]
